{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>They speak, utter emptiness</b> — a strange construction, as though the word is compounded from the adjacent verb and the non-adjacent one, or it was so because of a guttural letter. And the analogy is mishpat (justice), which is sweet, turned to bitter, like: who turn justice to wormwood. And it shall blossom — the fruit of their judgment which is not straight." "<b>Upon furrows</b> — like תלמיה (its furrow). רוה." "<b>And Shaddai</b> — like שדה (field). And the witness: יעלוז שדי."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:47.130708949Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}